      "text": "### Book Information\n\n**Title:** Stochastic Governance: Probabilistic Approaches to Policy Design Under Uncertainty  \n**Authors:** Vasilis Papadimitriou and Sakura Nishihara  \n**Year:** 2021  \n**Publisher:** MIT Policy Press  \n**ISBN:** 978-0-26203-847-1  \n**Summary:**  \nThis 312-page technical monograph applies Bayesian inference and stochastic optimization to the design of public policies under deep uncertainty. The authors argue that conventional policy analysis frameworks, which rely on deterministic projections and point estimates, systematically underperform in contexts characterized by non-stationary risks and contested model assumptions. They introduce the 'adaptive policy envelope' framework, treating policy commitments as probability distributions over outcome spaces rather than fixed prescriptions. This allows for policies to be revised in light of new evidence without undermining their credibility. The monograph includes three extended case studies focusing on climate adaptation policy in the Netherlands, pandemic response protocol design, and infrastructure investment under seismic risk.\n\n**Key Themes:**\n- Bayesian policy analysis\n- Deep uncertainty\n- Adaptive governance\n- Stochastic optimization\n- Policy design\n- Decision theory\n- Uncertainty quantification\n\n---\n\n### Author Information\n\n**Vasilis Papadimitriou**  \n- Position: Professor of Public Policy, Harvard Kennedy School  \n- Research Focus: Bayesian policy analysis, adaptive governance, deep uncertainty  \n- PhD: MIT Operations Research, 2003  \n- Notable Publications: \n  - Stochastic Governance (MIT Policy Press, 2021)\n  - \"Adaptive Policy Envelopes under Deep Uncertainty\" (Policy Sciences, 2018)\n  - \"Bayesian Updating in Multi-Stakeholder Policy Contexts\" (Journal of Policy Analysis and Management, 2015)\n- Additional Role: Co-editor of *Uncertainty and Governance: A Reader* (MIT Press, 2019)  \n[More about Vasilis Papadimitriou](https://example.com/authors/vasilis-papadimitriou)\n\n**Sakura Nishihara**  \n- No biography or specific information found in the search.\n\nIf you need further assistance or additional information, feel free to ask!",
      "mediaUrl": null
    }
